    "updated_at": "2026-10-14T10:32:27Z",
    "body": "> I think the fix is to expose the selected resource's dimensions directly. Reversing the density correction with the source size doesn't work anymore with [#13046](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13046): `naturalWidth` is exactly the `sizes` value for images selected with a `w` descriptor.\n> \n> Maybe `pixelWidth`/`pixelHeight` on both `HTMLImageElement` and `HTMLVideoElement`: the current resource's natural dimensions in image (or video) pixels. That's after orientation (and, for video, aspect-ratio correction), but before any density correction (from `srcset` or EXIF resolution). They'd be 0 if the image isn't available or has no natural dimensions.\n\n(bikeshedding) How about `sourceWidth` and `sourceHeight`?\nOr `selectedSource{Width|Height}` and `actualSource{Width|Height}` if we want to be explicit about what was selected by the srcset algorithm and what actually arrived?\n\nOtherwise this seems fine to me.",
