    "updated_at": "2026-10-14T12:49:04Z",
    "body": "Exposing a new property sounds good to me.\n\nOne thing I will note is that in Chrome Devtools, in the Elements tab, when hovering over an img element, the dialog popup includes the value that we desire and calls it intrinsic size.\n\nScreenshot attached ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d40e318c-43d1-4a38-ae43-3118cc2b628f)\n\n\nSee this article here: https://www.debugbear.com/docs/intrinsic-vs-rendered-size\n\nThis value is not density corrected but is the resources pixel width and height . Should we align on a name here to keep things consistent for developers? \n\nintrinsicWidth|Height",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
