    "updated_at": "2026-10-21T16:14:46Z",
    "body": "I just thought of something, we will likely also need to consider some equivalent \"hard pixel\" or \"actual pixel\" properties to `naturalWidth/naturalHeight` on `PerformanceElementTiming`\n\nChromium currently has a bug I believe and ships the intrinsic pixel size (we thought about taking advantage of this bug). core/paint/timing/element_timing.cc passes cached_image.IntrinsicSize(orientation), which is Image::Size, straight into the entry. No density anywhere. That is a spec deviation; it survived since 2019 because nobody tested srcset. Worth filing on w3c/element-timing so the raw value gets specced before someone “fixes” it. ",
